{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/228728-soul-infusion-on-mummies","id":228728,"title":"Soul Infusion on Mummies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-14T21:27:11-07:00","id":228728,"title":"Soul Infusion on Mummies","content":"Ok, so, I had thought I'd read somewhere that Mummies never lose consciousness. I think I may have been confused as a consequence of all the &quot;bashing/lethal damage doesn't render a Mummy unconscious&quot; bits though. As written, it looks like it's possible to drain Willpower from a Mummy until they fall unconscious, just like with any mortal. It seems a bit strange, given the nature of Arisen as undead and generally not losing consciousness in other circumstances, but without any evidence to the contrary I'm going to let my players do it. Has anyone found anything definitive either way that suggests whether powers like this can knock out Mummies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T09:26:37-07:00","id":229119,"title":"","content":"I remember one of the devs (CAS maybe?) saying conclusively that mummies do <i>sleep</i> during their descent, so I guess effects that essentially put them to sleep might work?<br /> <br /> I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:03:49-07:00","id":229657,"title":"","content":"Huh. I hadn't actually heard that. The fact that Mummies are Undead made me assume they didn't need to rest.<br /> <br /> The book could honestly be a bit more clear on the subject. There are occasional references to dreams, but Mummies are undead. There's no real guide in the book for what that means to them, but most of the Lifeless in the book have a clear explanation that includes &quot;don't need to rest&quot; (see Unnatural Toughness that Awakened Thralls and Nenitu have, for example). I've just been running with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 08-16-2014, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T15:21:40-08:00","id":328682,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure they don't need to sleep, but are capable of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T15:25:32-08:00","id":328688,"title":"","content":"We've been playing for a while now (see the Actual Play thread), ruling that Soul Infusion does indeed effect Mummies. And yes, that sleep is possible but not necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}